---
/**
 * GoogleMap.astro — a Google Maps embed, replacing the projected inline SVG.
 *
 * WHY THIS REPLACED CoverageMap/ServiceAreaMap
 * ===========================================
 * Ryan, August 2026: "change these maps out for Google maps instead, easier to
 * understand, site wide". A visitor recognises a Google map instantly and can
 * read a town off it without learning the legend first, which the stylised SVG
 * asked them to do.
 *
 * That reverses a deliberate decision, and the reasoning it reverses is worth
 * keeping in view rather than deleting. CoverageMap.astro was built against a
 * real failure: the site this replaces carried a Leaflet map that loaded,
 * rendered and centred on Saskatchewan, and nothing in that build could tell it
 * had gone wrong. Tile maps were then rejected on LICENSING — no keyless,
 * commercial-use tile provider could be vetted.
 *
 * That licensing objection does not apply to this one. Google's Maps Embed API
 * is free for commercial use with no usage cap, which is precisely what the
 * OSM, CARTO and Stamen basemaps could not offer. The geography objection does
 * not apply either: Google is being asked for a named place, not handed a
 * projection to get right.
 *
 * WHAT IS GIVEN UP, STATED PLAINLY
 *   · A third-party request on every page that renders a map, where there were
 *     none. Google sets cookies. There is no consent banner on this site.
 *   · The 49 market pins. A keyless embed shows one place, not a pin set.
 *     Those markets are still listed as links under every map by MarketIndex,
 *     which is the part a visitor can actually click.
 *   · First-paint rendering. This is an iframe, so it is lazy and it arrives
 *     after the text.
 *
 * The coverage is still stated in words beside the map, so the map is never the
 * only place a reader or a crawler can learn where Graduate works. That rule
 * survives the change and is the reason the caption is a required prop.
 *
 * NO API KEY. The `output=embed` form needs none. If Google ever withdraws it,
 * the documented replacement is the Embed API v1 with a free key, and this file
 * is the only place that changes.
 */
interface Props {
  /** The map's accessible name, used as the iframe title. Keep it a sentence. */
  label: string;
  /** Visible caption under the map. Required: the map is never the only source. */
  caption: string;
  /** Optional small heading above the map. */
  heading?: string;
  /** What Google is asked to show — a place name, not coordinates. */
  query: string;
  /** Google zoom level. 9 region, 11 borough, 12 town. */
  zoom?: number;
  /**
   * A Google My Maps id. When present the embed shows that custom map — which
   * is how all 49 market pins get onto one frame without an API key. When it is
   * empty the component falls back to the place-centred embed below, so a map
   * that has not been created yet renders correctly rather than blank.
   */
  mid?: string;
  class?: string;
}
const { label, caption, heading, query, zoom = 11, mid, class: klass } = Astro.props;

const src = mid
  ? `https://www.google.com/maps/d/embed?mid=${encodeURIComponent(mid)}`
  : `https://maps.google.com/maps?q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}&z=${zoom}&output=embed`;
---
<figure class:list={['gmap', klass]}>
  {heading && <p class="gmap-heading">{heading}</p>}
  <div class="gmap-frame">
    <iframe
      src={src}
      title={label}
      loading="lazy"
      referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"
      allowfullscreen
    ></iframe>
  </div>
  <figcaption>{caption}</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .gmap { margin: 1.8rem 0 2.2rem; }
  .gmap-heading {
    margin: 0 0 .6rem;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: .11em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }
  /* The box is sized before the iframe loads, so nothing reflows under the
     reader when it arrives. */
  .gmap-frame {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    max-height: 26rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--surface-alt);
  }
  @media (min-width: 700px) { .gmap-frame { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; } }
  .gmap-frame iframe {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border: 0;
    display: block;
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: .6rem;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
